                    Here is some information for remote desktop connection troubleshooting:
                        Common Errors:
                            Incorrect Computer Name:
                                Ensure the full name of the UTD computer is entered, which includes the department abbreviation and asset number (e.g., UTD81905).
                                Use the fully-qualified domain name (FQDN), such as UTD81905.campus.ad.utdallas.edu, rather than just the computer name.
                            
                            Computer Unavailable:
                                This occurs if the computer is powered off or not set up for remote access.
                                To check, ping the computer by running the command ping UTDAssetNumber.campus.ad.utdallas.edu in a terminal.
                                If the computer is unreachable, it may be off or disconnected from the network. Someone must power it on to resolve the issue.
                            
                            Access Denied:
                                This error indicates that you do not have remote desktop authorization.
                                Contact the OIT Service Desk for assistance.

